course: dictionary
lesson: 6583
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. «Nip» is a good example: it can mean a bite, a quick trip, or a chill in the air. The words around it tell you which meaning the writer wants, so read the whole sentence before you decide.
explain: «The puppy nipped my finger» tells you nip means a small, quick bite. But «Watch the twins while I nip to the shop,» says Mum is different: here nip means to go somewhere quickly for a short time. Ask yourself: does my meaning fit the other words in the sentence?
explain: Nip can also be a noun, a thing you can have, like «a nip in the air», which means a cold feeling. Phrases change the meaning again. «Nip it in the bud» means stop a problem early, before it grows. Never stop at the first meaning you think of.
fact: Nip can be a verb (to nip) or a noun (a nip).
fact: «Nip» means to give a small, quick bite or pinch, as a puppy does when it is playing.
fact: In British, Irish and Australian talk, «nip to the shop» means to go to the shop quickly for a short time.
fact: «A nip in the air» means it is getting cold, often in autumn.
fact: «Nip it in the bud» means stop a problem early, and «nip and tuck» means very close, as in a race.
exercise: «The puppy nipped my finger.» What does nipped mean here? | To wrap up warmly | *To give a small, quick bite | To sing a loud song
exercise: «Watch the twins while I nip to the shop,» says Mum. What does nip mean? | To take a long journey abroad | To bite hard | *To go somewhere quickly for a short time
exercise: Dad says, «There's a nip in the air, so get your coat.» What does a nip in the air mean? | It is hot and sunny | There is a bee nearby | *It is getting cold
test: In «I will nip upstairs for my book», what does nip mean? | *To go up quickly for a short time | To fall down the stairs | To sleep for a long time | To shout very loudly
test: Which phrase means to stop a problem early, before it grows? | Nip to the shop | *Nip it in the bud | A nip in the air | Nip and tuck
exam: In «She had a nip of brandy after dinner», what does nip mean? | A loud shout | A long walk in the park | A big sandwich | *A small amount of a strong drink
